fuzz: make Dataset::open return null instead of SEGV when H5Fopen fails

BAG::Dataset::readDataset() catches the H5File constructor's FileIException but
only LOGS it and falls through to `make_unique<Metadata>(*this)` with a null
m_pH5file. Metadata::Metadata(Dataset&) then calls getH5file() (`return
*m_pH5file;`) -> h5file.openDataSet(), dereferencing the null-bound reference and
crashing with a SEGV in bag_metadata.cpp. This happens for EVERY input that is
not a valid, openable HDF5/BAG file -- including the empty seed libFuzzer starts
from -- so both OSS-Fuzz harnesses crash on input #0 and the campaign can never
explore. (Upstream's `fuzzer` branch is trying to fix exactly this:
"Attempt to catch FileIException in BAG::Dataset::open()".)

Applied at BUILD TIME ONLY (mayhem/build.sh) so the upstream source in the repo
stays unmodified (the two-branch model keeps all repo changes additive). After
the existing catch, if the file did not open we throw the same FileIException
type that Dataset::open() already catches and turns into a `nullptr` return --
the exact behavior both harnesses are written to expect.

diff --git a/api/bag_dataset.cpp b/api/bag_dataset.cpp
index 730d442..1fa837e 100644
--- a/api/bag_dataset.cpp
+++ b/api/bag_dataset.cpp
@@ -1108,6 +1108,13 @@ void Dataset::readDataset(
         e.printErrorStack();
     }

+    // mayhem: if H5Fopen failed above, m_pH5file is null; constructing Metadata
+    // (which calls getH5file() -> *m_pH5file) would dereference null and SEGV.
+    // Rethrow so Dataset::open()'s catch returns nullptr, the contract both
+    // OSS-Fuzz harnesses already handle.
+    if (!m_pH5file)
+        throw ::H5::FileIException{"Dataset::readDataset", "unable to open file"};
+
     m_pMetadata = std::make_unique<Metadata>(*this);

     m_descriptor = Descriptor{*m_pMetadata};
